                                                "sense_id": "478b6674-0842-3386-8b88-df76040b8de9",
                                                "text": "Many religious leaders oppose cloning humans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe6c551e-2295-3185-93df-1593cb21e1a0",
                                        "entry_id": "39b1c92d-d4e7-3fb2-8117-dfe72914857b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To present or set up in opposition; to pose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5bb437c-7b8e-4a8a-8dbd-cd9b523a3bcd",
                                                "sense_id": "fe6c551e-2295-3185-93df-1593cb21e1a0",
                                                "text": "They are opposed to any form of hierarchy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9921a917-075c-448a-b050-c5b7285f7e3f",
                                                "sense_id": "fe6c551e-2295-3185-93df-1593cb21e1a0",
                                                "text": ", Book I\nI may […] oppose my single opinion to his."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bdfad5d-fdf5-4c29-9143-600b2d33563e",
                                                "sense_id": "fe6c551e-2295-3185-93df-1593cb21e1a0",
                                                "text": "[T]hree walls had been left standing, with large intervals between each; and they would certainly oppose a most formidable interruption to an invader."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82921eab-01d8-3928-b906-17c6f8c899f2",
                                        "entry_id": "39b1c92d-d4e7-3fb2-8117-dfe72914857b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To place in front of, or over against; to set opposite; to exhibit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29c7903d-f619-4c8c-aa04-789649ca7b01",
                                                "sense_id": "82921eab-01d8-3928-b906-17c6f8c899f2",
                                                "text": "Her grace sat down […] / In a rich chair of state; opposing freely / The beauty of her person to the people."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
